    "SERIES": "2026-Q1 Babel",
    "WORD": "CLEAN",
    "GLOSS": "Free from dirt, impurities, or moral blemish; purified and acceptable.",
    "CARD_TYPE": "ADJECTIVE",
    "RARITY_TEXT": "UNCOMMON",
    "RARITY_ICON": "UNCOMMON",
    "ART_PROMPT": "A glowing, pure drop of water falling into a still basin, creating perfect concentric ripples, surrounded by pristine white lilies and a bright, ethereal light.",
    "ABILITY_TEXT": "Target player reveals their hand. You may place up to 2 of those cards on the bottom of the Tower. If you do, that player draws that many cards.",
    "STAT_LORE": 3,
    "STAT_CONTEXT": 4,
    "STAT_COMPLEXITY": 2,
    "OT_VERSE_REF": "Psalm 51:10",
    "OT_VERSE_SNIPPET": "Create in me a clean heart, O God, and renew a right spirit within me.",
    "NT_VERSE_REF": "John 15:3",
    "NT_VERSE_SNIPPET": "Already you are clean because of the word that I have spoken to you.",
    "OT_VERSE_LINE": "Psalm 51:10 — “Create in me a clean heart, O God, and renew a right spirit within me.”",
    "NT_VERSE_LINE": "John 15:3 — “Already you are clean because of the word that I have spoken to you.”",
    "GREEK": "καθαρός",
    "GREEK_TRANSLIT": "katharos",
    "HEBREW": "טָהוֹר",
    "HEBREW_TRANSLIT": "tahor",
    "OT_REFS": "Lev 11:47 • Ps 24:4 • Ezek 36:25",
    "NT_REFS": "Matt 5:8 • John 13:10 • Titus 1:15",
    "TRIVIA_BULLETS": [
      "In the Old Testament, 'tahor' often referred to the ritual purity required to enter the Tabernacle or consume certain foods [1.8].",
      "In the New Testament, Jesus emphasized that true cleanness comes from within the heart, rather than just outward ceremonial washing.",
      "The Greek word 'katharos' is related to the English words 'chaste' and 'chasten,' reflecting a state free from corrupt desire or guilt."
